  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜たら: when (something that is going to happen)",
     "texto": [
      "With the **たら** form (past verb + **ら**) you talk about something that **is going to happen**: **ばんごはん を たべたら、 さんぽ を します** (when I've eaten dinner, I'll go for a walk).",
      "It is used a lot when the later action has not happened yet."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜たら: if (a condition)",
     "texto": [
      "For a condition or a future situation: **あめ が ふったら、 うち に います** (if it rains, I'll stay at home). It can also raise a hypothesis: **おかね が あったら、 にほん へ いきたい です** (if I had money, I'd like to go to Japan)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜なら: if that is the case…",
     "texto": [
      "**なら** picks up a situation or topic already mentioned: **にほん へ いく なら、 はる が いい です** (if you're going to Japan, spring is a good time). It's used to offer information or advice on that topic."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
